---

<DocsLayout
  title="LSP"
  subtitle="A practical reference for nikcli language-server discovery, startup, diagnostics, and the gated LSP tool."
  description="Reference for nikcli language-server discovery, startup, diagnostics, and the gated LSP tool."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      nikcli uses Language Server Protocol servers as an optional code-intelligence layer for tools,
      diagnostics, symbols, definitions, references, hover information, implementations, and call
      hierarchy. The service lives under <code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp</code> and is loaded through an
      Effect service, so every project instance gets its own LSP state, root detection, client list,
      and shutdown finalizer.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-grid not-prose">
      <DocCard title="Lazy by file" eyebrow="Startup">
        <p>Servers are not launched globally at boot. A file touch or operation selects matching servers by extension and then starts the needed client.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Per root" eyebrow="Workspace">
        <p>Each server chooses a root from lockfiles, language manifests, or the current instance directory. Clients are reused per server plus root pair.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Configurable" eyebrow="Config">
        <p>Built-in servers can be disabled or overridden, and custom servers can be added when their file extensions are declared.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Tool gated" eyebrow="Agent">
        <p>The agent-facing <code>lsp</code> tool is experimental and is only registered when the LSP tool flag is enabled.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="lifecycle" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Runtime lifecycle</h2>
    <p>
      The service state is created from the current instance context and current config. If
      <code>lsp</code> is set to <code>false</code>, the service keeps an empty server map and all
      operations become unavailable. Otherwise nikcli loads every built-in server from
      <code>LSPServer</code>, filters experimental servers, applies config overrides, and records a
      finalizer that shuts down every connected client when the instance is disposed.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Resolve config</strong> from global, project, and remote sources through <code>Config.defaultLayer</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Build the server map</strong> from <code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/server.ts</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Apply experimental filtering</strong>: <code>ty</code> replaces <code>pyright</code> only when the Python flag is set.</li>
      <li><strong>Merge overrides</strong>: disabled entries are removed; command overrides replace spawn behavior.</li>
      <li><strong>Spawn on demand</strong> when <code>touchFile</code>, <code>hasClients</code>, or an LSP operation needs a matching extension.</li>
      <li><strong>Initialize JSON-RPC</strong> with root URI, workspace folders, diagnostics, watched-file support, and configuration support.</li>
      <li><strong>Cache clients</strong> by root plus server id, mark broken pairs, and reuse in-flight spawns.</li>
      <li><strong>Dispose cleanly</strong> by ending the JSON-RPC connection and killing the child process.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="When a server starts">
      <p>
        A server starts the first time a matching file is touched by a debug command, status sync,
        or the agent-facing LSP tool. The service does not pre-launch every supported language.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="servers" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Supported servers</h2>
    <p>
      The built-in catalog is declared in <code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/server.ts</code>. Each entry
      has an id, extension list, root strategy, and spawn function.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Server ids</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>JavaScript and web</td><td><code>typescript</code>, <code>deno</code>, <code>eslint</code>, <code>oxlint</code>, <code>biome</code>, <code>vue</code>, <code>svelte</code>, <code>astro</code></td><td>TypeScript uses the workspace <code>typescript/lib/tsserver.js</code>. Deno only activates when a Deno config file is found.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Python</td><td><code>pyright</code>, <code>ty</code></td><td><code>ty</code> is hidden unless <code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_LSP_TY</code> is enabled; when enabled it disables <code>pyright</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Systems</td><td><code>rust</code>, <code>clangd</code>, <code>zls</code>, <code>terraform</code></td><td>Rust requires <code>rust-analyzer</code> in PATH. Several binary servers can auto-download into the nikcli bin directory.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JVM and .NET</td><td><code>jdtls</code>, <code>kotlin-ls</code>, <code>csharp</code>, <code>fsharp</code></td><td>Java requires Java 21 or newer for JDTLS. .NET languages install tools through <code>dotnet tool</code> when allowed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Other languages</td><td><code>gopls</code>, <code>ruby-lsp</code>, <code>elixir-ls</code>, <code>sourcekit-lsp</code>, <code>yaml-ls</code>, <code>lua-ls</code>, <code>php intelephense</code>, <code>prisma</code>, <code>dart</code>, <code>ocaml-lsp</code>, <code>bash</code>, <code>texlab</code>, <code>dockerfile</code>, <code>gleam</code>, <code>clojure-lsp</code>, <code>nixd</code>, <code>tinymist</code>, <code>haskell-language-server</code></td><td>Many use PATH first, then nikcli-managed binaries, then optional auto-install depending on the server.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="roots" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Root detection</h2>
    <p>
      Root selection is server-specific. Most entries use <code>NearestRoot</code>, which walks upward
      from the file directory toward the current nikcli instance directory and returns the directory
      containing a matching marker file. If no marker exists, some servers fall back to the current
      instance directory; others return no root and do not start.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Examples</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Package roots</td><td><code>bun.lock</code>, <code>package-lock.json</code>, <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code>, <code>yarn.lock</code></td><td>Used by TypeScript, web framework servers, YAML, and format/lint servers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Language manifests</td><td><code>Cargo.toml</code>, <code>go.mod</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>mix.exs</code>, <code>composer.json</code></td><td>Keep language servers scoped to the real project or module root.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace-aware roots</td><td><code>go.work</code>, Rust workspace <code>Cargo.toml</code>, Gradle settings files</td><td>Prefer multi-module roots before module-local fallbacks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fixed instance roots</td><td><code>bash</code>, <code>dockerfile</code></td><td>Use the active nikcli directory directly.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="agent-tool" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Agent tool</h2>
    <p>
      The <code>lsp</code> tool in <code>packages/nikcli/src/tool/lsp.ts</code> exposes editor-like
      navigation to agents. It accepts a file path, one-based line and character values, asks for
      <code>lsp</code> permission, opens the file through the LSP client, waits briefly for
      diagnostics, and then runs the selected operation.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Protocol request</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>goToDefinition</code></td><td><code>textDocument/definition</code></td><td>Find the declaration or implementation target for a symbol.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>findReferences</code></td><td><code>textDocument/references</code></td><td>Return all references, including declarations.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>hover</code></td><td><code>textDocument/hover</code></td><td>Read type or documentation information at a position.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>documentSymbol</code></td><td><code>textDocument/documentSymbol</code></td><td>List symbols for one document.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>workspaceSymbol</code></td><td><code>workspace/symbol</code></td><td>Search project symbols and keep the top ten class/function-like results.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>goToImplementation</code></td><td><code>textDocument/implementation</code></td><td>Find implementations of interfaces or abstract members.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>prepareCallHierarchy</code></td><td><code>textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy</code></td><td>Prepare the call hierarchy item for a function or method.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>incomingCalls</code></td><td><code>callHierarchy/incomingCalls</code></td><td>Find callers after preparing call hierarchy.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>outgoingCalls</code></td><td><code>callHierarchy/outgoingCalls</code></td><td>Find callees after preparing call hierarchy.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="The tool is experimental">
      <p>
        The agent tool is registered only when <code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_LSP_TOOL</code> is enabled,
        or when global experimental mode enables experimental tools. Without that gate the service
        can still power debug/status flows, but the agent cannot call <code>lsp</code>.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="debug" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Debug commands</h2>
    <p>
      The debug command group touches files and prints raw LSP JSON responses. Use it to check
      whether root detection, server startup, and diagnostics are working before relying on agent
      calls.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
nikcli debug lsp diagnostics packages/nikcli/src/lsp/index.ts
nikcli debug lsp symbols Session
nikcli debug lsp document-symbols file:///absolute/path/to/file.ts
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Diagnostics waits for a publish event after opening the file, sleeps briefly, and then prints
      the collected diagnostics map. Symbol commands call the service directly and print JSON.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="configuration" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Configuration</h2>
    <p>
      The <code>lsp</code> config field accepts <code>false</code> to disable all language servers, or
      a server-id map to disable, override, or add servers. Custom server ids must declare
      <code>extensions</code>, because nikcli otherwise cannot know which files should start them.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Applies to</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>lsp = false</code></td><td>All servers</td><td>Disable the LSP service for the current config scope.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lsp.SERVER.disabled = true</code></td><td>Built-in or custom</td><td>Remove a server from the enabled map.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lsp.SERVER.command</code></td><td>Override or custom</td><td>Command array used to spawn the server process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lsp.SERVER.extensions</code></td><td>Override or custom</td><td>File extensions that activate the server. Required for unknown ids.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lsp.SERVER.env</code></td><td>Override or custom</td><td>Environment variables merged into the server child process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>lsp.SERVER.initialization</code></td><td>Override or custom</td><td>Initialization options passed during initialize and configuration requests.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>Dot-path config sketch</h3>
    <DocCode language="text">
lsp.typescript.disabled = true
lsp.my-language.command = my-language-server --stdio
lsp.my-language.extensions = .my, .mine
lsp.my-language.env.MY_LANGUAGE_MODE = strict
lsp.my-language.initialization.workspaceMode = full
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="downloads" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Downloads and binaries</h2>
    <p>
      Some servers require a system binary in PATH. Others install language-server packages or
      release binaries into <code>Global.Path.bin</code>, which resolves to the <code>bin</code>
      directory under nikcli's data root. Auto-downloads are skipped when
      <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_LSP_DOWNLOAD</code> is set.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Resolution path</th><th>Examples</th><th>Operational note</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>PATH only</td><td><code>deno</code>, <code>rust-analyzer</code>, <code>dart</code>, <code>gleam</code>, <code>ocamllsp</code></td><td>Install the binary yourself before using the file type.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bun package install</td><td><code>pyright</code>, <code>svelte-language-server</code>, <code>@astrojs/language-server</code>, <code>bash-language-server</code></td><td>nikcli installs into its data bin area when downloads are allowed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Release archive</td><td><code>clangd</code>, <code>zls</code>, <code>lua-ls</code>, <code>terraform-ls</code>, <code>texlab</code>, <code>tinymist</code></td><td>Archives are fetched, extracted, marked executable, and reused.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Language toolchain</td><td><code>gopls</code>, <code>rubocop</code>, <code>csharp-ls</code>, <code>fsautocomplete</code></td><td>Requires the matching language toolchain, such as Go, Ruby, or .NET.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="diagnostics" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Diagnostics and symbols</h2>
    <p>
      When a file is opened, nikcli sends <code>workspace/didChangeWatchedFiles</code> and
      <code>textDocument/didOpen</code>. If the same file is touched again, it sends a watched-file
      change plus <code>textDocument/didChange</code> with an incremented version. Published
      diagnostics are normalized to filesystem paths and stored per client.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Diagnostics debounce</strong> waits for the matching path and server id, then resolves after a short quiet period.</li>
      <li><strong>TypeScript first diagnostic quirk</strong> suppresses the first TypeScript publish event when the file had no diagnostic entry yet.</li>
      <li><strong>Workspace symbols</strong> filter to classes, functions, methods, interfaces, variables, constants, structs, and enums.</li>
      <li><strong>Document symbols</strong> accept a file URI and return raw document or location symbols after filtering empty values.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>No LSP server available for this file type.</code></td><td>No enabled server matched the extension, or root detection returned no root.</td><td>Check the extension, language manifest, and <code>lsp</code> config overrides.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Server never starts</td><td>Required binary is missing, download is disabled, or the language toolchain is absent.</td><td>Install the binary or unset <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_LSP_DOWNLOAD</code> for supported auto-download servers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Server starts once and then stays unavailable</td><td>The root plus server id was marked broken after spawn or initialize failed.</td><td>Fix the binary/config issue and dispose or restart the nikcli instance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Diagnostics are empty</td><td>The server did not publish diagnostics within the wait window, or the file opened before analysis completed.</td><td>Run the diagnostics debug command again, or check the language server logs and project root.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tool call denied</td><td>The agent-facing tool asks for <code>lsp</code> permission.</td><td>Approve the request or update the session permission rules.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Python server differs from expected</td><td><code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_LSP_TY</code> switches Python from <code>pyright</code> to <code>ty</code>.</td><td>Unset the flag for pyright or install <code>ty</code> for the experimental path.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="source-anchors" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Source anchors</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What to inspect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/index.ts</code></td><td>Effect service, config merging, client cache, operations, and status.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/client.ts</code></td><td>JSON-RPC connection, initialize payload, open/change notifications, diagnostics handling, shutdown.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/server.ts</code></td><td>Built-in server catalog, root detection, spawn commands, downloads, experimental Python server selection.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/lsp/language.ts</code></td><td>File extension to language id mapping used when opening documents.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/tool/lsp.ts</code></td><td>Agent tool parameters, permission request, one-based to zero-based position conversion, and operation dispatch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/debug/lsp.ts</code></td><td>Diagnostics and symbol debug commands.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/config/config.ts</code></td><td><code>lsp</code> schema, validation, and custom-server extension requirement.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
